ion and sorting invariance.\n   - `monotone_prop` / `monotone_thm`: output cut points are sorted in non-decreasing order (`List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·)`) for both `\"inclusive\"` and `\"exclusive\"` methods.\n   - `inclusive_bounds_prop` / `inclusive_bounds_thm`: for `\"inclusive\"`, every cut point lies between the minimum and maximum of `data`.\n   - `pointwise_prop` / `pointwise_thm`: exact pointwise linear interpolation specification for every index `k < n - 1`.\n   - `constant_data_prop` / `constant_data_thm`: constant datasets with value `c` produce `List.replicate (n - 1) c`.\n   - `shift_equivariant_prop` / `shift_equivariant_thm`: translation equivariance under `x ↦ x + c`.\n   - `benchmark_quantilesReal_ratCast_thm` & `benchmark_quantilesReal_spec_thm`: `ℚ`-to-`ℝ` cast correspondence and `ℝ`-layer specification.\n4. **Post-condition, PBTs, and Correctness Theorem ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L917-L1121))**:\n   - `Post_prop` combining the verified properties, tested via both randomized Plausible checks (`#eval Plausible.Testable.check ...`) and bounded `native_decide` PBTs, and proved in `benchmark_quantiles_correct`.\n5. **Imperative Implementation & Equivalence ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L1127-L1310))**:\n   - `quantiles_imp`, `benchmark_quantiles_imp`, `quantilesFloat_imp`, and `benchmark_quantilesFloat_imp` using `Id.run do` and mutable loop state, tested and proved equivalent to the functional implementations in `quantiles_equiv`, `benchmark_quantiles_equiv`, `quantilesFloat_equiv`, and `benchmark_quantilesFloat_equiv`."}
